# Architecture

The Security Monitoring and Threat Detection Lab consists of multiple security monitoring components working together to collect, process, store, and analyze security events.

## Data Flow

Internet Attack Traffic
↓
Cowrie Honeypot
↓
Wazuh Agent
↓
Wazuh Manager
↓
OpenSearch Indexer
↓
Wazuh Dashboard
↓
Security Monitoring

## Components

### Cowrie Honeypot
Generates attack telemetry by simulating an exposed SSH service.

### Wazuh Agent
Collects and forwards logs for analysis.

### Wazuh Manager
Processes events, applies rules, and generates alerts.

### OpenSearch Indexer
Stores and indexes security events.

### Wazuh Dashboard
Provides alert visualization and analyst access.

### Tailscale
Provides secure remote administration through a Zero Trust network model.
